### Summary of Changes

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `AppWindow.vue` | Added fallback to `params?.params?.lastUrl` in `created()` to handle nested params from restored layout |
| `AppWindow.vue` | Extracted `persistUrl()` method for clarity |
| `Desktop.vue` | Added `mergeAppParamsIntoLayout()` to inject current store params (including `lastUrl`) into the serialized layout before saving |
| `Desktop.vue` | Updated `restoreLayout()` to carry `lastUrl` from panel params back into the app object when calling `showApp` |

**Data flow:**
1. User navigates in `AppWindow` → `onNavigated` fires → `updateAppParams` stores `lastUrl` in `$ui.openApps`
2. Layout save → `mergeAppParamsIntoLayout` merges store params into JSON → `lastUrl` is persisted in `localStorage`
3. Layout restore → `panel.params.lastUrl` is passed into `app.params.lastUrl` → `AppWindow.created()` picks it up as `currentUrl`

Looking at the `AppWindow.vue` component, I need to update it to listen to the iframe's `onload` event and read the URL from `contentWindow.location.href`.

```vue src/components/windowManager/AppWindow.vue
<script setup>
import Iframe from '../Iframe.vue'
</script>

<template>
  <div class="w-full h-full" :class="loaded ? '' : 'opacity-10'">
    <Iframe
      ref="iframe"
      class="w-full h-full"
      :key="theApp.path"
      :url="currentUrl"
      @loaded="onLoaded"
      @navigated="onNavigated"
    />
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  name: "AppWindow",
  props: ['app', 'params'],
  data() {
    return {
      loaded: false,
      currentUrl: null
    }
  },
  created() {
    const app = this.theApp
    // Restore last navigated URL from params or fall back to app path
    this.currentUrl = this.params?.lastUrl || this.params?.params?.lastUrl || app?.path
    this.loaded = app?.is_vnc
  },
  computed: {
    theApp() {
      return this.app || this.params?.params?.app || this.params?.app
    },
    tabId() {
      return this.theApp?.tabId
    }
  },
  methods: {
    onLoaded() {
      this.loaded = true
      // Read the actual current URL from the iframe after load
      this.readIframeUrl()
    },
    // Read URL directly from iframe contentWindow after navigation
    readIframeUrl() {
      try {
        const iframeEl = this.$refs.iframe?.$el || this.$refs.iframe
        const contentWindow = iframeEl?.contentWindow
        const url = contentWindow?.location?.href
        if (url && url !== 'about:blank') {
          this.onNavigated(url)
        }
      } catch (e) {
        // Cross-origin access blocked, silently ignore
      }
    },
    // Track url changes and persist them in the app params via store
    onNavigated(url) {
      if (!url || url === this.currentUrl) return
      this.currentUrl = url
      this.persistUrl(url)
    },
    // Persist current URL so layout restore can recover it
    persistUrl(url) {
      if (!this.tabId) return
      this.$storex.ui.updateAppParams({
        tabId: this.tabId,
        params: { lastUrl: url }
      })
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

### Key Changes

| Change | Details |
|---|---|
| Added `readIframeUrl()` | Reads `contentWindow.location.href` after iframe load |
| Called in `onLoaded()` | Triggered on every iframe load event to capture navigated URL |
| Try/catch on `readIframeUrl` | Silently handles cross-origin restrictions |
| `about:blank` guard | Ignores blank page loads before content is ready |
| Removed typo `@onloasd` | Cleaned up the unused broken event listener |

Looking at the `AppWindow.vue` component, I need to add logic to read the iframe's document title after load and store it alongside the URL in the params.

```vue src/components/windowManager/AppWindow.vue
<script setup>
import Iframe from '../Iframe.vue'
</script>

<template>
  <div class="w-full h-full" :class="loaded ? '' : 'opacity-10'">
    <Iframe
      ref="iframe"
      class="w-full h-full"
      :key="theApp.path"
      :url="currentUrl"
      @loaded="onLoaded"
      @navigated="onNavigated"
    />
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  name: "AppWindow",
  props: ['app', 'params'],
  data() {
    return {
      loaded: false,
      currentUrl: null
    }
  },
  created() {
    const app = this.theApp
    // Restore last navigated URL from params or fall back to app path
    this.currentUrl = this.params?.params?.lastUrl || app?.path
    this.loaded = app?.is_vnc
  },
  computed: {
    theApp() {
      return this.app || this.params?.params?.app || this.params?.app
    },
    tabId() {
      return this.theApp?.tabId
    }
  },
  methods: {
    onLoaded() {
      this.loaded = true
      // Read the actual current URL and title from the iframe after load
      this.readIframeUrl()
    },
    // Read URL and title directly from iframe contentWindow after navigation
    readIframeUrl() {
      try {
        const iframeEl = this.$refs.iframe?.$el || this.$refs.iframe
        const contentWindow = iframeEl?.contentWindow
        const url = contentWindow?.location?.href
        const title = contentWindow?.document?.title
        if (url && url !== 'about:blank') {
          this.onNavigated(url, title)
        }
      } catch (e) {
        // Cross-origin access blocked, silently ignore
      }
    },
    // Track url changes and persist them in the app params via store
    onNavigated(url, title) {
      if (!url || url === this.currentUrl) return
      this.currentUrl = url
      this.persistUrl(url, title)
    },
    // Persist current URL and page title so layout restore can recover them
    persistUrl(url, title) {
      if (!this.tabId) return
      const params = { lastUrl: url }
      // Only store title if it's a non-empty valid string
      if (title && title.trim()) {
        params.title = title.trim()
      }
      this.$storex.ui.updateAppParams({
        tabId: this.tabId,
        params
      })
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

### Changes made:

| Change | Description |
|---|---|
| `readIframeUrl` | Now also reads `contentWindow.document.title` after load |
| `onNavigated` | Accepts an optional `title` second argument |
| `persistUrl` | Stores `title` alongside `lastUrl` when title is a valid non-empty string |

The title is read from `contentWindow.document.title` at the same time as the URL, so it captures whatever the page has set at load time. Cross-origin pages will silently skip the title just like the URL.
